---
// The homepage. Every terminal transcript on it is real croft 0.1.0 output, from the project the Quickstart builds
// (docs/quickstart.md shows the same runs), trimmed only where a line says so.
import version from '../generated-version.json'
import mark from '../assets/mark.svg?raw'

const title = 'croft: data pipelines your agent can run'
const description =
  'Local data pipelines in TypeScript, on one DuckDB file. Ingest APIs and files, transform with SQL or TypeScript, keep the tables fresh, and let Claude Code drive it all.'
const canonical = new URL('/', Astro.site).href

// Braces in a template's text start an expression, so code samples with braces are strings.
const stripeCharges = `<span class="cm">// assets/stripe_charges.ts</span>
export default ingest({
  key: <span class="s">"id"</span>,
  incremental: {
    field: <span class="s">"created"</span>, unit: <span class="s">"s"</span>,
    lookback: <span class="s">"30 days"</span>,
  },
  schedule: <span class="s">"every hour"</span>,
  async *rows({ since, http }) { … },
});`
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/plain" href="/llms.txt" title="croft docs, for agents" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <script is:inline>
      // Follow the theme chosen in the docs (Starlight stores it as starlight-theme), else the system's.
      try {
        const t = localStorage.getItem('starlight-theme')
        if (t === 'light' || t === 'dark') document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t
      } catch {}
    </script>
    <style is:global>
      :root {
        --ground: #f6f3ea;
        --raised: #fffdf7;
        --sunk: #ece7da;
        --ink: #1b1a16;
        --ink-2: #4a463c;
        --ink-3: #7a7466;
        --rule: #ddd6c6;
        --green: #2f6b3e;
        --green-2: #3f8a52;
        --green-wash: #dfeee2;
        --ochre: #b8741f;
        --term: #191814;
        --term-ink: #e9e4d6;
        --term-dim: #9a9381;
        --term-ok: #8fd19e;
        --term-err: #f08b7a;
        --term-key: #e8b765;
        --mono: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', 'JetBrains Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        --sans: ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Inter, Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
        color-scheme: light;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root:not([data-theme='light']) {
          --ground: #141411;
          --raised: #1c1b17;
          --sunk: #11100e;
          --ink: #f1ede2;
          --ink-2: #c7c1b2;
          --ink-3: #8f8979;
          --rule: #2f2d27;
          --green: #7cc28c;
          --green-2: #95d4a3;
          --green-wash: #1d3022;
          --ochre: #e0a24a;
          --term: #0d0d0b;
          color-scheme: dark;
        }
      }
      :root[data-theme='dark'] {
        --ground: #141411;
        --raised: #1c1b17;
        --sunk: #11100e;
        --ink: #f1ede2;
        --ink-2: #c7c1b2;
        --ink-3: #8f8979;
        --rule: #2f2d27;
        --green: #7cc28c;
        --green-2: #95d4a3;
        --green-wash: #1d3022;
        --ochre: #e0a24a;
        --term: #0d0d0b;
        color-scheme: dark;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--ground);
        color: var(--ink);
        font: 16px/1.6 var(--sans);
        text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
      }
      a { color: var(--green); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
      code, pre { font-family: var(--mono); }
      .wrap { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding-inline: 1.25rem; }
    </style>
    <style>
      /* ── header ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      header { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding-block: 0.9rem; }
      .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55rem; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 650; font-size: 1.15rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
      .brand :global(svg) { width: 1.6rem; height: 1.6rem; display: block; }
      nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.25rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
      nav a { color: var(--ink-2); text-decoration: none; }
      nav a:hover { color: var(--ink); }

      /* ── hero ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .hero > * { min-width: 0; }
      .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: 3rem; align-items: center; padding-block: 4.5rem 4rem; }
      .eyebrow { font: 600 0.8rem/1 var(--mono); color: var(--ochre); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 4.6vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -0.035em; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-weight: 720; }
      h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--green); }
      .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 1.75rem; max-width: 34rem; }
      .install { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; padding: 0.7rem 0.7rem 0.7rem 1rem; max-width: min(30rem, 100%); }
      .install code { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; white-space: nowrap; overflow-x: auto; }
      .install code::before { content: '$ '; color: var(--ink-3); }
      .copy { font: 600 0.8rem/1 var(--sans); border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--ground); color: var(--ink-2); border-radius: 7px; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem; cursor: pointer; }
      .copy:hover { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink-3); }
      .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
      .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 9px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.97rem; }
      .btn.primary { background: var(--green); color: var(--ground); }
      .btn.primary:hover { background: var(--green-2); }
      .btn.ghost { color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .btn.ghost:hover { border-color: var(--ink-3); }
      .needs { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--ink-3); }

      /* ── terminal ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
      .term { background: var(--term); color: var(--term-ink); border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.04), 0 18px 50px -24px rgba(20, 30, 20, 0.55); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }
      .term-top { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); }
      .term-top i { width: 0.6rem; height: 0.6rem; border-radius: 50%; background: #3a3832; }
      .term-top span { margin-left: 0.5rem; font: 0.75rem var(--mono); color: var(--term-dim); }
      .term pre { margin: 0; padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.2rem; font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.6; overflow-x: auto; }
      .term .p { color: var(--term-dim); }
      .term .c { color: var(--term-ink); font-weight: 600; }
      .term .ok { color: var(--term-ok); }
      .term .err { color: var(--term-err); }
      .term .k { color: var(--term-key); }
      .term .d { color: var(--term-dim); }

      /* ── sections ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
      section { padding-block: 4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); letter-spacing: -0.025em; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 0.9rem; font-weight: 700; }
      .sub { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 1.08rem; max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 0 2.25rem; }
      .three { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; }
      .card { background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.4rem 1.4rem 1.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
      .card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
      .card .tag { font: 600 0.72rem/1 var(--mono); color: var(--ochre); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
      .card p { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.97rem; }
      .card pre { margin: auto 0 0; background: var(--sunk); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.55; overflow-x: auto; color: var(--ink); }
      .card pre .cm { color: var(--ink-3); }
      .card pre .s { color: var(--green); }
      .card a.more { margin-top: 0.9rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }

      .tree { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: 2.5rem; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 2.75rem; }
      .tree pre { margin: 0; background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.75; overflow-x: auto; }
      .tree pre .cm { color: var(--ink-3); }
      .tree pre b { color: var(--green); font-weight: 600; }
      .tree ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
      .tree li { padding-left: 1.4rem; position: relative; color: var(--ink-2); }
      .tree li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.62em; width: 0.55rem; height: 0.55rem; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--green); }
      .tree li strong { color: var(--ink); }

      .agent { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; }
      .agent .term pre { font-size: 0.74rem; }
      .label { font: 600 0.78rem/1.3 var(--sans); color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
      .points { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem 2.5rem; margin: 2.25rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .points li { color: var(--ink-2); }
      .points strong { color: var(--ink); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }
      .points code, .sub code, .safe code, .tree code { font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--sunk); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; color: var(--ink); }

      .safe { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.9rem 2.5rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
      .safe li { padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem; background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.97rem; }
      .safe strong { color: var(--ink); }

      .stack { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--raised); }
      .stack div { padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem; }
      .stack div + div { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .stack .was { font: 0.82rem var(--mono); color: var(--ink-3); text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-color: var(--ochre); }
      .stack .now { font-weight: 650; margin-top: 0.3rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
      .stack p { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.93rem; }
      .nots { margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.98rem; }

      .end { text-align: center; padding-block: 4.5rem; }
      .end .install { margin: 1.5rem auto 0; }
      .end .ctas { justify-content: center; }

      footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: 1.75rem 2.5rem; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 0.88rem; }
      footer .wrap { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; justify-content: space-between; }
      footer a { color: var(--ink-2); }
      footer .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem; }

      @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .hero, .tree, .agent { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        .hero { padding-block: 3rem; gap: 2.25rem; }
        .three { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        .stack { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        .stack div + div { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      }
      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .points, .safe { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        nav .optional { display: none; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <div class="wrap bar">
        <a class="brand" href="/"><Fragment set:html={mark} />croft</a>
        <nav aria-label="Main">
          <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
          <a href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
          <a class="optional" href="/docs/reference/cli/">Reference</a>
          <a class="optional" href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/Zabaca/croft">GitHub</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <div class="wrap hero">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">croft {version.version} · MIT</p>
          <h1>Data pipelines <em>your agent can run.</em></h1>
          <p class="lede">
            croft pulls data from APIs and files, transforms it with SQL or TypeScript, and keeps the tables fresh, all
            in one DuckDB file on your machine. It is one CLI, and Claude Code can drive it from a cold start.
          </p>
          <div class="install">
            <code id="install">bun add -g @zabaca/croft</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="install">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <div class="ctas">
            <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart →</a>
            <a class="btn ghost" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
          </div>
          <p class="needs">Needs Bun 1.3.14+ on macOS or Linux. No Python, no Docker, no server.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="term" role="img" aria-label="A croft session: validate, preview and run a SQL transform">
          <div class="term-top"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>~/my-data</span></div>
          <pre><span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">croft validate</span>
checked 2 assets in 98 ms
<span class="ok">0 errors, 0 warnings</span>

<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">croft preview revenue_by_region</span>
Preview: your real tables are not changed.
revenue_by_region 4 rows (new table)   +4 added · 0 removed
  <span class="k">columns</span>  region VARCHAR · orders BIGINT · revenue DOUBLE
  <span class="k">checks</span>   <span class="ok">ok</span> unique(region) · <span class="ok">ok</span> not_null(region) · <span class="ok">ok</span> revenue &gt; 0
  <span class="k">sample</span>   region  orders  revenue
           East    50      2637.5
           North   17      885.5

<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">croft run revenue_by_region</span>
run r_1018_0045_ecsl · 1 asset
<span class="ok">ok</span>       revenue_by_region  4 rows (57 ms) · new table, 3 columns
                            added 4 · updated 0 · checks 4/4 ok
done 57 ms · 1 updated · 0 failed
<span class="d">next: croft query "from revenue_by_region limit 5"</span></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section>
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>One folder. One file per table.</h2>
          <p class="sub">
            Each file in <code>assets/</code> makes one table with the file's name, and <code>croft run</code> brings them
            up to date. A table that reads an updated table is rebuilt after it, in the same run. croft reads the
            dependencies from your SQL; there is no DAG to declare.
          </p>
          <div class="tree">
<pre>my-data/
  croft.json
  assets/
    <b>stripe_charges.ts</b>   <span class="cm"># ingest: Stripe, incremental</span>
    <b>sales.ts</b>            <span class="cm"># ingest: CSV exports</span>
    <b>daily_revenue.sql</b>   <span class="cm"># transform: one SELECT</span>
    <b>lead_scores.ts</b>      <span class="cm"># transform: LLM per row</span>
  lib/                  <span class="cm"># shared code</span>
  warehouse.duckdb      <span class="cm"># every table, one file</span></pre>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Every write is all-or-nothing.</strong> Checks run on the rows before they are saved; a failed check writes nothing and the table keeps its data.</li>
              <li><strong>Types are inferred, schema changes handled.</strong> New fields appear as columns, nested objects become JSON, and real conflicts fail loudly with the fix.</li>
              <li><strong>Apps read it directly.</strong> <code>import {'{'} query {'}'} from "@zabaca/croft/read"</code> works under Bun and Node, through <code>croft serve</code> when one is running.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="three">
            <div class="card">
              <div class="tag">Ingest · the dlt part</div>
              <h3>APIs and files</h3>
              <p>Cursor, keyset, Link-header and page pagination; CSV, JSON and Parquet, globs and URLs. Incremental with a lookback for records that change.</p>
<pre set:html={stripeCharges} />
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/ingest/">Ingests →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="tag">Transform · the SQLMesh part</div>
              <h3>SQL or TypeScript</h3>
              <p>One SELECT per file, with checks in the header. Or TypeScript per row, such as an LLM call that is incremental and never re-bills a row.</p>
<pre><span class="cm">-- assets/revenue_by_region.sql</span>
<span class="cm">-- key: region</span>
<span class="cm">-- check: revenue > 0</span>
SELECT region,
       count(*)    AS orders,
       sum(amount) AS revenue
FROM example_sales
GROUP BY region</pre>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/sql/">SQL transforms →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="tag">Keep fresh · the Dagster part</div>
              <h3>Schedules in plain words</h3>
              <p>One per-user OS job runs what is due. Transforms follow their inputs. The scheduler only runs code a person has run by hand.</p>
<pre><span class="p">$</span> croft validate
duckdb_releases: daily at 6am
  (cron 0 6 * * *); next
  2026-10-18 06:00,
  2026-10-19 06:00, …

<span class="p">$</span> croft schedule on</pre>
              <a class="more" href="/docs/guides/scheduling/">Scheduling →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Built for the agent. Guarded for you.</h2>
          <p class="sub">
            Every command takes <code>--json</code>. Every problem has a stable code, a hint with the literal next
            command, and often a fix the agent can apply as is. Anything destructive stops and waits for a person.
          </p>
          <div class="agent">
            <div>
              <p class="label">A typo, caught before anything runs, with the edit that fixes it</p>
              <div class="term">
                <div class="term-top"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>croft validate</span></div>
                <pre><span class="err">error UNKNOWN_COLUMN</span>  assets/revenue_by_region.sql:8:7
      Referenced column "ammount" not found in FROM clause.
      <span class="k">fix:</span> replace ammount with amount on line 8

<span class="p">$</span> <span class="c">croft validate --json</span>
<span class="d">…</span> "fix": {'{'}
      "kind": "edit",
      "file": "assets/revenue_by_region.sql",
      "line": 8,
      "replace": {'{'} "from": "ammount", "to": "amount" {'}'}
    {'}'} <span class="d">…</span></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="label">A destructive step, stopped until the person says yes</p>
              <div class="term">
                <div class="term-top"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>croft delete duckdb_releases</span></div>
                <pre><span class="k">needs confirmation:</span> delete duckdb_releases,
  the whole table: 64 rows
  first: the 64 rows go to the trash
    (croft restore duckdb_releases brings them back)
  ask the user; if they agree:
    croft confirm c_8ef55d    (valid 15 min)
<span class="err">error CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED</span>  duckdb_releases
      effect: nothing was changed
<span class="d">exit 5</span></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="points">
            <li><strong>A skill in every project.</strong> <code>croft init</code> writes the croft skill and a <code>CLAUDE.md</code> block, stamped with the project's pinned version.</li>
            <li><strong>One permission rule.</strong> Every destructive path ends in <code>croft confirm</code>, so <code>"ask": ["Bash(croft confirm:*)"]</code> gates them all.</li>
            <li><strong>A loop that touches no data.</strong> <code>validate</code> binds every SELECT against its inputs' columns without running anything; <code>preview</code> builds in a sandbox and diffs.</li>
            <li><strong>Docs offline, and here as Markdown.</strong> <code>croft docs</code> has a page for every error code. This site serves <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> and a <code>.md</code> twin of every page.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Nothing implicit destroys your data.</h2>
          <p class="sub">Ingested data may be impossible to fetch again. So croft never refetches or deletes it on its own.</p>
          <ul class="safe">
            <li><strong>Deleting an asset file</strong> leaves its table in place.</li>
            <li><strong>Changing an ingest's key or cursor</strong> stops the run and asks how to go on.</li>
            <li><strong>An API that suddenly returns nothing</strong> trips the shrink guard instead of wiping the table.</li>
            <li><strong>Rebuilds, deletes and restores</strong> go to the trash first; <code>croft restore</code> brings them back.</li>
            <li><strong>A half-finished edit</strong> is held by the scheduler until a person runs it once.</li>
            <li><strong>A crash, even <code>kill -9</code></strong>, never leaves half a write. Cursors move only on commit.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Three tools' jobs, in one CLI.</h2>
          <p class="sub">For people who are not data engineers and who build with an agent. No compatibility with their formats, and no jargon to learn.</p>
          <div class="stack">
            <div><div class="was">dlt</div><div class="now">ingest()</div><p>APIs and files into typed tables, incremental, with schema changes handled.</p></div>
            <div><div class="was">SQLMesh</div><div class="now">.sql and transform()</div><p>Transforms with checks, rebuilt when their code or inputs change.</p></div>
            <div><div class="was">Dagster</div><div class="now">schedule: "every hour"</div><p>A schedule in plain words, and transforms that follow their inputs.</p></div>
          </div>
          <p class="nots">Everything else is Bun and one DuckDB library. <code>bun.lock</code> is the whole environment.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="end">
        <div class="wrap">
